<h2>Shiloh Square Beaded Inset on the Island</h2>

<p>The island is where the <strong>Square Beaded Inset</strong> shows off. Look at the close-up below — the bead is routed around every door and drawer opening, doors sit flush in the frame, and the reveal stays consistent panel-to-panel. This is one of <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry">Shiloh's</a> trademark moves, and unlike most semi-custom shops, beaded inset is priced the same as overlay. No upcharge, no extended lead time. Same boxes, more refined faces.</p>

<p>Calinia Henry paired the bead detail with leather pull knobs on the column of small drawers — the kind of detail that takes a stock door style and makes it feel like a custom build.</p>

