<h2>Flush Inset on the Pantry Run</h2>

<p>The corner pantry/hutch run is built in <strong>Flush Inset</strong> — the cleaner, harder-to-execute cousin to beaded inset. Doors sit dead flush with the face frames, the stiles get tighter, and the reveals are pencil-thin. There's nowhere to hide a misalignment. This is the kind of cabinet detail that designers and homeowners point at and say <em>"that's the level of finish I want"</em> — and now 5 Blox has it sitting in the showroom in the exact finish people are asking about.</p>

